WEBVTT

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:21.450
<b>Muhyo & Roji's
Bureau of Supernatural Investigation</b>

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:38.490
I'm sure I just saw the two 
of them go through here.

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:40.740
But...

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:10.340
Snow?

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:24.240
W-Wow!

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:26.250
N-Nana-chan?

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:29.250
What are you doing here?

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:32.020
I followed you.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:35.750
D-cups...

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:46.810
You didn't tell me you were bringing along
 a busty little beauty like this, Muhyo!

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:49.210
Who the hell is this?!

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:50.600
Just an idiot.

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:54.250
I'm Yoichi, a judge. Nice to meet you.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:01.110
<b>Article 4 
Omen</b>

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:09.750
Hey, so where are we? A foreign country?

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:13.880
I wonder the same thing 
every time I come here.

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:17.930
But no, we're in Japan, Nana-chan.

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:22.160
It's apparently somewhere in the mountains 
of Azumino, in Nagano Prefecture.

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:23.070
Mountains?

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:26.590
Yeah. The Association bought this 
land, including the mountains,

00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:30.790
and packed all its magical law 
agencies into it, like a town.

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:35.270
You must be cold! Here's a cape.

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:38.320
Your shoulders are so soft.

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:43.200
How about a romantic date with me 
in this snowy town, Nana-chan?

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.370
No way! Don't get so cozy with me!

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:48.170
Well, in any case,

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:52.390
this town isn't exactly an ideal 
environment for dates anymore.

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:55.580
Don't you agree, Muhyo?

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:01.530
Every last person here...

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:04.300
looks so damn gloomy.

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:07.460
And we have Enchu to thank for it.

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:11.380
<i>What is this uneasy feeling I'm having?</i>

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:15.280
Y-Yoichi-san, is Enchu-san—

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:16.770
Hey, Roji.

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:19.800
I need to speak with him.

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:22.780
Stay with Nana until you hear 
the exam registration bell.

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:26.510
Once that's over, see that she gets home.

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:29.640
Nana-chan, let's go on a date sometime!

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:31.020
Bleh!

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:34.920
You haven't told Roji

00:04:35.590 --> 00:04:37.420
about him yet, have you?

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:41.690
About Enchu, I mean.

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:48.100
Wait, Nana-chan!

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:51.310
Wow! Western film style?

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:54.640
Dutch style?

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:56.900
Japanese style?

00:04:57.610 --> 00:04:58.690
A well?

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:01.940
What's the deal with this mixed-up town?!

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:08.360
MLS?

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:10.480
It stands for "Magic Law School."

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:12.670
It's a school of magical law.

00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:15.560
What? There's a school of magical law?

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:20.160
Yeah. Muhyo and Yoichi-san started 
here when they were kids.

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:21.550
And you didn't?

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:23.930
I applied several times, 
but I didn't make it...

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:26.760
Bye, Sensei!

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:29.430
So those kids must be pretty elite, huh?

00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:31.960
Oh, some of them look foreign.

00:05:32.670 --> 00:05:35.760
There are people all around 
the world who can see spirits.

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:38.260
It's a highly competitive school.

00:05:38.260 --> 00:05:39.940
Hey!

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:42.620
I heard the genius Muhyo is in town!

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:45.940
What? The youngest executor, Muhyo?!

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:48.760
Wow! Let's go find him!

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:52.080
You're teamed up with a pretty 
important partner, huh?

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:52.700
Yeah.

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:55.830
<i>I have to do well on this exam.</i>

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:57.100
I'm going home!

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:57.960
Why?

00:05:58.220 --> 00:06:02.380
My mom said that if Muhyo 
shows up, Enchu will, too!

00:06:03.790 --> 00:06:07.050
Enchu? Yoichi-san mentioned that name, too.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:09.960
When I was still in training...

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:12.220
There was a magic lawyer 
I was good friends with.

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:19.160
Although he got jealous of my talent 
and ran off to the dark side.

00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:23.300
The magic lawyer Muhyo was talking about

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:25.180
must have been Enchu.

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:38.120
It's been a while since we came 
to this restaurant together.

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:40.410
Since that one time, huh?

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:45.560
Two executors have been killed by evil 
spirits since the start of this month.

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:46.130
Lily Elena

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:46.130
Okouchi Sosei

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:49.560
Lily Elena and Okouchi Sosei.

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:50.010
Lily Elena

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:51.930
Both were renowned executors.

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:53.470
Okouchi Sosei

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:56.760
This is more than just a 
simple act of evil spirits.

00:07:03.510 --> 00:07:05.440
Even the Magical Law Association

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:08.790
is stressing over which magical lawyers 
to send after what evil spirits.

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:13.560
I didn't come here to listen 
to a stupid story like that.

00:07:14.770 --> 00:07:15.950
I know.

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:18.400
You want to know what he's up to.

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:19.960
I've been looking into it.

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:23.840
Our classmate from MLS, now a traitor...

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:26.110
Enchu is probably hiding

00:07:26.110 --> 00:07:28.460
somewhere here in the Shin'etsu region.

00:07:33.990 --> 00:07:36.040
What is this place?!

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:39.220
This is the Magical Law Library.

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:43.900
It has every book ever 
published on magical law

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:48.480
as well as regular books, for 
a total of 30 million books.

00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:51.990
It's actually foggy near the top!

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:57.080
Hey... Roji-kun?

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:58.490
Wait up!

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:02.490
<i>The back issues of </i>Magical Law 
Journal<i> must be here somewhere...</i>

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:05.080
<b>Magical Law Journal</b>

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:05.080
<b>The Youngest Executor Ever!</b>

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:05.080
<b>Muhyo Toru Special</b>

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:05.080
<b>Young Talent
Appears!</b>

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:05.080
<b>A Shock Wave Rattles the 
World of Magical Law!!</b>

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:10.710
Oh, there they are!

00:08:11.350 --> 00:08:12.760
Let's see...

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:15.510
The issues that had Muhyo in them...

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:19.000
Huh?

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:20.820
What?

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:23.640
They're gone...

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:25.770
All the issues that had Muhyo in them are gone.

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:37.910
<i>That scared me.</i>

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:39.320
<i>Is that a guy?</i>

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:41.990
<i>Those pretty facial features...</i>

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:52.800
<i>A scar on the back of the neck...</i>

00:08:54.150 --> 00:08:55.300
Oh, there you are!

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:05.440
That's the exam registration 
commencement bell!

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:11.420
Jeez, Roji-kun, what's up with you?

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:20.150
Is this... Muhyo-san?

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:28.960
Wh-Why...

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:43.160
Your presence at this information 
session with your executor

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:47.910
officially confirms your 
participation in tomorrow's exam.

00:09:48.310 --> 00:09:50.750
There will be both written
 and practical sections,

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:53.360
and the key to earning 
a promotion will be...

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:56.190
Ah, there they are!

00:09:56.770 --> 00:09:59.910
What was he thinking, leaving 
a girl alone like that?

00:10:03.380 --> 00:10:06.090
<i>What was that all about before?</i>

00:10:06.090 --> 00:10:07.900
<i>I want to tell them about it,</i>

00:10:07.900 --> 00:10:09.980
<i>but I'll have nothing to 
do until this is over...</i>

00:10:10.450 --> 00:10:12.300
<i>Maybe I'll look for Yoichi-san.</i>

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:15.880
<i>Wait, no! No way! 
He's the enemy of women!</i>

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:17.770
<i>Get your head on straight, Nana!</i>

00:10:18.280 --> 00:10:20.140
Hey, Nana-chan.

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:24.340
I'm glad to see that cape suits you so well.

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:27.240
Wh-What do you want?

00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:30.050
Just so you know, I won't 
go on a date with you!

00:10:30.050 --> 00:10:33.000
Aw, you're no fun.

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:36.650
And I came all this way looking for you.

00:10:39.770 --> 00:10:41.900
But, you know...

00:10:42.850 --> 00:10:46.100
Aren't those guys down there 
in the exam hall kinda noisy?

00:10:56.260 --> 00:10:57.960
That voice...

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:03.970
<b>Hades's Banquet</b>

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:03.970
<b>Muhyo & Roji's Bureau of 
Supernatural Investigation</b>

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:09.980
<b>Ferry Ride Across the Styx</b>

00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:09.980
<b>Muhyo & Roji's Bureau of 
Supernatural Investigation</b>

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:12.390
But, you know...

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:16.580
Aren't those guys down there 
in the exam hall kinda noisy?

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:35.460
Nana-chan, what happened?!

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:38.550
Huh?

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:41.380
Nana-chan, what's wrong?

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:49.480
H-Huh? I know I saw...

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:50.440
What's this?

00:11:51.720 --> 00:11:54.310
Well, if it isn't Judge Yoichi.

00:11:54.760 --> 00:11:58.860
You shouldn't be in here scaring girls.

00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:01.900
I'm trying to give information on the exam.

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:04.950
Darn, I guess you found me.

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:06.870
Guess that date's on hold.

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:13.500
And since you're here, why don't you 
stay and observe the exam hall?

00:12:17.110 --> 00:12:19.500
Okay... I'll do that.

00:12:22.180 --> 00:12:23.260
Quiet.

00:12:23.560 --> 00:12:26.220
Don't touch it. It'll transfer to you.

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:27.520
Huh?

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:31.860
A spirit's infected the three of them.

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:38.320
P-Please shake my hand, Yoichi-san!

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:41.570
Okay, sure. Here you go.

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:43.680
Good luck on the exam.

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:44.860
Thank you!

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:46.070
Me next!

00:12:49.170 --> 00:12:51.500
E-Executor Muhyo!

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:53.410
M-M-M-May...

00:12:53.720 --> 00:12:55.420
May I have your autograph?

00:12:59.570 --> 00:13:00.490
Hmph.

00:13:01.970 --> 00:13:04.560
Yeah, of course it wouldn't work...

00:13:04.560 --> 00:13:06.010
He's scary!

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:07.430
So cool, though!

00:13:07.730 --> 00:13:10.750
Wow, that's amazing.

00:13:10.750 --> 00:13:13.750
These guys are idols of the 
magical law world, huh?

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:16.440
That's true.

00:13:17.320 --> 00:13:19.320
<i>Th-This is awful...</i>

00:13:19.780 --> 00:13:22.320
<i>How many people has it already spread to?</i>

00:13:25.590 --> 00:13:27.900
He shook my hand!

00:13:29.010 --> 00:13:31.880
All right, everyone, please take your seats.

00:13:31.880 --> 00:13:34.550
I'm going to continue the explanation.

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:38.830
<i>Muhyo, what are you going to do?</i>

00:13:39.680 --> 00:13:42.590
Listen to me. Don't make a fuss over this.

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:45.640
Spirits that infect people like this

00:13:45.640 --> 00:13:48.330
spread even further through chaos.

00:13:49.330 --> 00:13:51.400
What are we going to do, then?

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:56.230
Use magical law to strike the original 
spirit that's hiding somewhere.

00:13:57.040 --> 00:14:01.560
Until then, don't scream, 
no matter what happens.

00:14:04.520 --> 00:14:09.200
<i>Or so he said, but when is he going 
to actually </i>use<i> magical law?</i>

00:14:16.070 --> 00:14:18.090
<i>Oh, I get it!</i>

00:14:18.090 --> 00:14:21.290
<i>It would cause a commotion 
if he used it in this crowd,</i>

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:23.900
<i>so he's already started it in secret!</i>

00:14:23.900 --> 00:14:25.710
<i>Muhyo, you're a genius!</i>

00:14:26.560 --> 00:14:30.970
<i>Let me see. The sentence for 
infecting people should be...</i>

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:36.980
Demon Prosecutor | Advent of Hades | Hades' Banquet 
| Purification by Boiling | Spirit Striker | Inferno

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:32.620
<i>Here it is!</i>

00:14:32.620 --> 00:14:34.860
<i>The magical law for finding 
the original spirit</i>

00:14:34.860 --> 00:14:36.980
<i>behind the infection and sentencing it!</i>

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:42.980
<b>Beginner</b>

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:42.980
<b>Let's 
Try 
Magical Law</b>

00:14:37.660 --> 00:14:40.590
<i>All right! I'll prepare a talisman</i>

00:14:40.590 --> 00:14:42.980
<i>so I can be ready to help Muhyo when—</i>

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:44.230
Hey.

00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:48.650
You're nervous about the exam, 
aren't you, Roji-kun?

00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:53.990
When that happens, you should 
close your books and just relax.

00:14:54.900 --> 00:14:55.990
<i>Oh, no!</i>

00:14:56.440 --> 00:14:57.190
Okay?

00:15:11.130 --> 00:15:13.260
<b>Spirit Striker</b>

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:13.260
<b>Spirit</b>

00:15:44.370 --> 00:15:45.320
<i>Huh?</i>

00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:46.750
<i>What?</i>

00:15:47.730 --> 00:15:49.660
<i>Nothing's happening to me.</i>

00:15:51.270 --> 00:15:54.510
What're you fidgeting for, Roji?

00:15:58.080 --> 00:16:01.200
Y-Yoichi-san...

00:16:01.200 --> 00:16:01.890
Roji?

00:16:02.280 --> 00:16:04.790
Y-Y-Your hand...

00:16:14.370 --> 00:16:17.780
Idiot. I told you not to scream.

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:20.920
What is that?!

00:16:20.920 --> 00:16:21.980
M-Mouths!

00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:23.790
They're over here, too!

00:16:26.370 --> 00:16:28.170
Damn! When did that happen?!

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:32.010
Help me!

00:16:38.740 --> 00:16:40.600
Everyone, don't panic!

00:16:45.510 --> 00:16:46.810
Yoichi-san!

00:16:46.810 --> 00:16:51.150
Until then, don't scream, 
no matter what happens.

00:16:52.180 --> 00:16:54.230
<i>This is my fault.</i>

00:16:55.730 --> 00:16:58.060
<i>I interfered with Muhyo.</i>

00:17:06.630 --> 00:17:07.210
<i>Huh?</i>

00:17:10.140 --> 00:17:11.540
I-It's gone...

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:13.500
Thank goodness!

00:17:14.400 --> 00:17:15.720
What was that?

00:17:18.040 --> 00:17:20.660
The original spirit should be defeated,

00:17:20.660 --> 00:17:23.110
so why is the magical law still in effect?

00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:25.740
It looks like...

00:17:26.240 --> 00:17:29.730
this is going to turn into a real mess.

00:17:50.470 --> 00:17:52.960
Please evacuate at once!

00:17:52.960 --> 00:17:55.630
Tomorrow's exam will be postponed.

00:17:56.050 --> 00:17:58.380
You will be contacted with the new date.

00:18:00.500 --> 00:18:02.890
Th-The magical law disappeared?

00:18:03.860 --> 00:18:06.180
Did it and the spirit take each other out?

00:18:06.850 --> 00:18:10.150
That's impossible! The messenger 
from Hell, fighting a spirit?

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:13.100
And we don't even know 
where this all started.

00:18:13.100 --> 00:18:15.080
Something's definitely fishy.

00:18:16.340 --> 00:18:18.190
Does this mean...

00:18:18.190 --> 00:18:19.750
Hey, Muhyo-san!

00:18:20.740 --> 00:18:22.160
It's Roji-kun!

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:25.410
Roji-kun took off!

00:18:27.400 --> 00:18:31.430
He said, "I can't get in 
Muhyo's way anymore."

00:18:32.240 --> 00:18:33.940
Oh, dear...

00:18:34.480 --> 00:18:36.330
Of all the times for him to...

00:18:36.330 --> 00:18:39.300
He's such a pain in my ass, I swear!

00:18:39.630 --> 00:18:41.960
I'll bring him back.

00:18:41.960 --> 00:18:44.460
Muhyo, you can wait at the inn.

00:18:44.460 --> 00:18:45.220
Hmph!

00:18:54.580 --> 00:18:56.090
Hey!

00:18:56.920 --> 00:18:58.780
Roji, you gloomy Gus!

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:00.940
Come hang out for a bit before you go!

00:19:08.690 --> 00:19:10.430
I'm sorry about your neck.

00:19:10.430 --> 00:19:12.970
Huh? Oh, this?

00:19:12.970 --> 00:19:16.090
Scratches like this happen all the 
time when you deal with spirits.

00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:18.640
You can't freak out over every—

00:19:19.730 --> 00:19:23.000
It's... my fault.

00:19:28.440 --> 00:19:31.770
If I hadn't screamed then,

00:19:32.310 --> 00:19:34.170
you and all the others

00:19:34.630 --> 00:19:36.660
wouldn't have gotten hurt.

00:19:38.070 --> 00:19:41.660
I don't have the confidence 
to stay with Muhyo anymore.

00:19:42.900 --> 00:19:46.990
I don't have the least bit 
of talent in magical law.

00:19:47.970 --> 00:19:50.500
Talent, huh?

00:19:53.350 --> 00:19:57.450
Muhyo told me not to tell 
you about this guy, but...

00:19:59.940 --> 00:20:02.940
Just think of this as me talking to myself.

00:20:04.290 --> 00:20:07.260
The guy was obsessed with talent. Yes...

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:09.970
<b>Madoka Soratsugu</b>

00:20:08.520 --> 00:20:10.100
Madoka Soratsugu,

00:20:09.970 --> 00:20:13.020
<b>Enchu</b>

00:20:10.770 --> 00:20:12.150
also known as Enchu.

00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:19.760
We were all classmates at MLS.

00:20:19.760 --> 00:20:22.150
We hung out together all the time.

00:20:38.660 --> 00:20:40.830
How do you think Roji felt when—

00:20:40.830 --> 00:20:41.920
Shut up.

